meta {
  name: 01 Get Subscription
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/subscription
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
}

docs {
  The business's current subscription client record (proxied from the subscription
  server's `GET /clients/show`). Returns `null` in `data` when the business is not
  yet registered — the frontend then shows the **Register Subscription** button.

  The record (when present) carries `name`, `code`, address fields, `pan_number` /
  `gst_number`, contact details, and a nested `plan` ({ title, slug, start_date,
  end_date, features_json }) or `false` when no plan is attached yet.

  Tenant (→ business id) comes from the JWT. Throws `SUBSCRIPTION_NOT_CONFIGURED`
  (503) when the integration is unconfigured, or `SUBSCRIPTION_BUSINESS_ID_MISSING`
  (409) when the tenant has no integer business id.
}
